# Chess knowledge pack - chess pieces (lesson 02)
#
# Taxonomy, count per side, and starting squares of every piece.

# --- Taxonomy ---
a_chess_piece is_part_of chess
the_king is a chess_piece
the_queen is a chess_piece
the_rook is a chess_piece
the_bishop is a chess_piece
the_knight is a chess_piece
the_pawn is a chess_piece

# Each side (white / black) has the same set
white_pieces is_part_of chess
black_pieces is_part_of chess
white_pieces resembles black_pieces

# --- Count per side ---
the_king has_count one_per_side
the_queen has_count one_per_side
the_rook has_count two_per_side
the_bishop has_count two_per_side
the_knight has_count two_per_side
the_pawn has_count eight_per_side

# Total pieces per side = 16
each_side shows 16_pieces

# --- Starting squares (White; Black mirrors on ranks 7-8) ---
the_king starts_on e1_white_e8_black
the_queen starts_on d1_white_d8_black
the_rook starts_on a1_h1_white_a8_h8_black
the_bishop starts_on c1_f1_white_c8_f8_black
the_knight starts_on b1_g1_white_b8_g8_black
the_pawn starts_on rank_2_white_rank_7_black

# Piece values (relative importance)
the_king shows infinite_value
the_queen shows value_9
the_rook shows value_5
the_bishop shows value_3
the_knight shows value_3
the_pawn shows value_1
